        "original_id": "56a378dc-8e49-52eb-ac70-746c348afe27",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tiffany Renee Darwish, The Beatles\n- Works: \"Could've Been\", \"I Saw Him Standing There\", \"I Saw Her Standing There\", \"Please Please Me\"\n- Topics: music careers, cover songs, chart performance\n\nFacts:\n- The Beatles released \"I Saw Her Standing There\" as the opening track on their 1963 debut album \"Please Please Me\".\n- Tiffany Renee Darwish was born on October 2, 1971, and she is an American singer, songwriter, actress, and former teen icon.\n- Tiffany Renee Darwish is also known professionally as Tiffany.\n- Tiffany released the singles \"Could've Been\" and \"I Saw Him Standing There\".\n- Tiffany's \"I Saw Him Standing There\" is a cover version of The Beatles' song \"I Saw Her Standing There\".\n- Tiffany's single \"Could've Been\" reached number one on the Billboard Hot 100.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
